               \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-5}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n![](images/96/96bd60d23237f836b77a26c5c0461a5c2a474554f0a14266b53fc5e7d999f1b7.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n* The domain of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n* The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\n\n* The period of $sin⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cc2ce46-b2a6-56de-8ead-93675bda43d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236005} {:answer/id #uuid "86f59763-455d-5124-95ad-635362b1efd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236659} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3a6054-cf44-59c2-a27b-e541dd8834c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236710} {:answer/id #uuid "e741a1bd-1d6c-5121-875f-22abed90b858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237269} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe8aa25-895a-5b00-b727-a03ec675ff51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cc2ce46-b2a6-56de-8ead-93675bda43d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236005} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a50de25-7441-55af-a64b-83272a0b732e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237577}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4817b633-1cdd-52d9-b9a7-098236a7867f" :question/math-academy-id "q-103230" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$\n\n- The function is zero at $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$\n- Its range is $y\\in [-2,2]$\n- $y=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is an output of the function" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. At $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$, the function $y=cos⁡x$ takes the value zero.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. The range of the function $y=cos⁡x$ is $y\\in [-1,1].$ Thus, $y=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is not an output of this function."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13cf2350-5cb8-5bce-82d7-7d69855b39b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235935} {:answer/id #uuid "3656391b-7c11-597f-a2bd-8b6a0f95faaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236162} {:answer/id #uuid "431b8b2c-60f9-50ed-a73e-335785cc18ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236250} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c131e4-70f4-5b57-9ffb-981148d71879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236948} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d7012c-5356-5c36-b422-e156f9cbdec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2c131e4-70f4-5b57-9ffb-981148d71879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236948} :answer-field/id #uuid "49b37897-7ab2-5034-96e3-b9f2f4798c3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237534}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4afb86c8-970f-594e-bb88-36f6e2c3e725" :question/math-academy-id "q-103233" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The zeros of the function are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi $\n- Its graph passes through the point $(0,1)$\n- The function has maximum values at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…,$ which can be written as $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. At $x=0,$ the function has the value $y=cos⁡0=1.$ Therefore, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,1).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a maximum at $x=0,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=2n\\pi .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043c68c8-e391-5780-a3ff-6d80dc52b081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290656} {:answer/id #uuid "931ab8d4-be2c-5e4d-92d6-fc6433eec3f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291265} {:answer/id #uuid "9767e111-d1e9-5924-9dc2-6f58d60a1d5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218629129